  "chapter": 6,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "SNG.6.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:SNG.6.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Whither is thy beloved gone, O thou fairest among women? whither is thy beloved turned aside? that we may seek him with thee.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "SNG.6.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:SNG.6.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "My beloved is gone down into his garden, to the beds of spices, to feed in the gardens, and to gather lilies.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "SNG.6.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:SNG.6.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "am",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " my beloved's, and my beloved ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " mine: he feedeth among the lilies.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "SNG.6.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:SNG.6.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thou ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "art",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " beautiful, O my love, as Tirzah, comely as Jerusalem, terrible as ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "an army",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " with banners.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "SNG.6.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:SNG.6.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Turn away thy eyes from me, for they have overcome me: thy hair ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " as a flock of goats that appear from Gilead.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "SNG.6.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:SNG.6.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thy teeth ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " as a flock of sheep which go up from the washing, of which every one beareth twins, and ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "there is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " not one barren among them.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "SNG.6.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:SNG.6.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "As a piece of pomegranate ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " thy temples within thy locks.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "SNG.6.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:SNG.6.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "There are sixty queens, and eighty concubines, and virgins without number.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "SNG.6.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:SNG.6.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "My dove, my undefiled is ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "but",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " one; she ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "only",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " one of her mother, she ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the choice ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "one",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " of her that bore her. The daughters saw her, and blessed her; ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "yes",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", the queens and the concubines, and they praised her.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "SNG.6.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:SNG.6.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Who ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " she ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " looketh forth as the morning, fair as the moon, clear as the sun, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " terrible as ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "an army",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " with banners?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "SNG.6.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:SNG.6.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I went down into the garden of nuts to see the fruits of the valley, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " to see whether the vine flourished, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the pomegranates budded.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "SNG.6.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:SNG.6.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Or ere I was aware, my soul made me ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "like",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the chariots of Amminadib.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "SNG.6.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:SNG.6.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Return, return, O Shulamite; return, return, that we may look upon thee. What will ye see in the Shulamite? As it were the company of two armies.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
